//! `control-operator-unsupported` uses two shell commands with `&&`.
//!
//! A shell block runs one command per statement.
//! The lowering refuses shell blocks before it reaches this form.
//!
//! The source puts `true && false` in one statement.
//!
//! - see: #1057 — `both`

/// `both` uses `&&` between two commands.
@[refuses("OutOfFragment.shell_block")]
def both() -> -F Unit { #!{ true && false; } }
